# Pairs with NoResurrection. Reproduces current production (#4503): once the
# old copy of a completed resize is purged, a routed operation on it is no
# longer refused. A read answers as the empty tree (the purge cleared its
# rows, PrepareForReadAsync with purgedAnswersEmpty), so a router that cached
# the old pair is served nothing for a key the resized copy holds. The edit
# lies in RoutedRefused, an operator the read path and the routed actions
# share, not in one action, so the mutation declares no PERTURBS.
MODULE: NoResurrectionPurgedCopyServesEmpty
TARGET: NoResurrection
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a routed read on the purged old copy answers empty, below an acknowledged value

--- FIND
RoutedRefused(c, s, k) == SplitRejects(c, s, k) \/ Fenced(c, s) \/ Redirected(c) \/ Gone(c)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a purged copy does not refuse routed operations.
RoutedRefused(c, s, k) == SplitRejects(c, s, k) \/ Fenced(c, s) \/ Redirected(c)
--- END
